n addition, the company is involved in the mining of iron ore; production of pellets and direct reduced iron; and processing of ferrous scrap through primary steelmaking and downstream finishing, stamping, tooling, and tubing. It serves direct automotive, infrastructure and manufacturing, distributors and converters, and steel producers. The company was formerly known as Cliffs Natural Resources Inc. and changed its name to Cleveland-Cliffs Inc. in August 2017. Cleveland-Cliffs Inc. was founded in 1847 and is headquartered in Cleveland, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. C. Lourenco Goncalves | CEO & Chairman | Age 67 | Compensation: $5.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 25K people. Revenue per employee of $744K ranks in the above the sector median among Basic Materials peers, improving at 14%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Cleveland-Cliffs Inc. is a mid-cap basic materials business with a $6.5B market cap on $18.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -7% over the past three years and +25% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 20% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $1.0B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 14.5% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.1pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 18% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 67% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6687262357414447},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.8M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2774815.79},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 89% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Cleveland-Cliffs (NYSE:CLF) Share Price Breaks Below 200-Day Moving Average \u2013 Should You Sell?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/cleveland-cliffs-nyseclf-share-price-bre